  <datafield tag="590" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Getty copy signed by the artist at colophon and numbered "81, from set #7, panel 9 out of 12." Front cover panel contains lint. Back cover has the word 'swarm' as well as 'insect.'</subfield>
  </datafield>
  <datafield tag="500" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
    <subfield code="a">Front cover has recessed panel containing either hair or lint from contributors listed on p. [4]-[5]. Text comprises color images and letterpress lists of possessions discarded by the artist. Back cover reproduces 1 of 12 panels with hand-drawn repetitions of the word 'insects' together with one of the words from the sentence 'Someday I will be as insignificant as a swarm of summer insects.' See p. [3]  &amp; [26].</subfield>
